 "final_result": "Built a three-script Python workflow for rutile TiO2 (mp-2657, P4_2/mnm #136) from scratch.\n\nWORKFLOW:\n1. generate_cif fetched TiO2 (mp-2657, P4_2/mnm #136) into structures/TiO2_base.cif (12 atoms). Reduced to primitive cell via chem_llm.kpath.kp_atoms(standard_kpath(atoms)): 12 -> 6 atoms (Ti2O4), space group unchanged.\n2. generate_structures.py: wrote 51 structures (structure_000.cif to structure_050.cif). Structure 000 is unperturbed; 001-050 have Gaussian thermal displacements (T=300K, rutile stable at RT; Ti RMS=0.17 A, O RMS=0.19 A, per-axis) plus random symmetric lattice strain (max 0.1%). nat=6, ntyp=2 asserted per structure.\n3. Pseudopotentials: Ti and O, norm-conserving, pbesol, stringent, UPF, scalar relativistic (Z=22,8 < 54, no spin-orbit needed). Ti z_valence=12 (semicore 3s2 3p6), O z_valence=6. Total electrons = 48, occupied bands = 24. Cutoffs: Ti 42 Ha = 84 Ry, O 46 Ha = 92 Ry -> ecutwfc=92 Ry, ecutrho=368 Ry (INVARIANT 5: 1 Ha = 2 Ry).\n4. setup_jobs.py: for each structure, created calculations/NNN/ with pseudopotentials, kpath.json, pw.in (SCF, kpts=6x6x9 Monkhorst-Pack via scf_kmesh), bands.in (NSCF, kpts=kp_kpts(kp), nbnd=48), bands_post.in (bands.x, lsym=.false.). Both pw.in and bands.in validated with validate_qe_input (nat/ntyp consistent, all variables in correct namelists).\n5. run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000: success (scf 19.9s, bands_scf 43.1s, bands_post 6.3s). SCF confirmed 48 electrons, 24 occupied bands, nbnd=48 sufficient.\n6. plot_bands.py: used chem_llm.kpath.plot_axis for x-axis/ticks/segments, chem_llm.qe_output.read_pw_out for n_occupied, band_edges for VBM/CBM. Aligned to VBM (semiconductor, occupations='fixed'). Saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nRESULTS:\n- Band gap: 1.847 eV (PBEsol, consistent with expected ~1.77 eV from MP)\n- VBM: 8.999 eV, CBM: 10.846 eV (raw QE energies)\n\nASE FUNCTIONS USED:\n- ase.io.read / ase.io.write for CIF I/O\n- ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in for pw.x input files\n- ase.Atoms for structure representation\n- chem_llm.kpath (standard_kpath, kp_atoms, kp_kpts, kp_save, scf_kmesh, plot_axis) for k-path and plotting\n- chem_llm.qe_output (read_pw_out, band_edges) for QE output parsing\n\nSCIENTIFIC ASSUMPTIONS:\n- T=300K for thermal displacements: rutile is the stable phase at room temperature (up to ~860 C)\n- Scalar relativistic pseudopotentials: Z=22 (Ti), Z=8 (O) both < 54, no spin-orbit physics targeted\n- occupations='fixed': clear semiconductor (gap ~1.8 eV), no smearing needed\n- ecutwfc=92 Ry (max of Ti and O recommendations), ecutrho=4x ecutwfc\n- nbnd=48 (2x occupied bands of 24) for safe padding\n- Debye-model estimate for thermal displacement amplitudes (simplified, not from phonon calculation)\n\nEXPERT REVIEW NEEDED:\n- The thermal displacement amplitudes are Debye-model estimates, not from a phonon calculation. For production-quality structures, one should use phonon-derived displacement parameters.\n- The band gap of 1.847 eV is a DFT-PBEsol value; the experimental gap is ~3.0 eV. For quantitative gap predictions, a hybrid functional (HSE06) or GW correction would be needed.",
